      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: require exact claims for direct cloud cleanup",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- require canonical lease IDs before DigitalOcean, Linode, Vultr, or Scaleway resources enter Crabbox inventory\n- require exact provider/account-or-project/resource-bound local claims before reuse, stop, or cleanup\n- keep claimless canonical resources read-only until explicit `--reclaim` adoption; never synthesize destructive ownership from remote tags\n- preserve interrupted-create recovery while validating the exact stored provider identity, and prevent read-only resolve paths from writing claims\n- document the ownership boundary in provider and stop documentation\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/811\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go test -race ./internal/providers/digitalocean ./internal/providers/linode ./internal/providers/scaleway ./internal/providers/vultr -count=1` — pass.\n- Focused CLI/provider race tests for exact claims, canonical-ID alias denial, and read-only status resolution — pass.\n- `go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/providers/digitalocean ./internal/providers/linode ./internal/providers/scaleway ./internal/providers/vultr` — pass.\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh` — pass; 53 command docs, 71 provider-matrix rows, 207 Markdown files, and the generated docs site verified.\n- Exact-branch autoreview — clean after fixing stale-claim status handling (0.79).\n- All 11 exact-head hosted checks pass, including Go, Release Check, Apple VZ, and CodeQL.\n\n## Exact-head live proof\n\nCandidate: `5a2ba9dd6314b638198e6a2928b3914c18865dfd`\n\n- DigitalOcean: authenticated from empty inventory; provisioned a real Droplet and managed SSH key; reached ready; ran `echo ok` over SSH; listed and stopped the exact claim; verified final inventory `[]` and no managed-key residue.\n- Linode: authenticated from empty inventory; provisioned a real instance; reached ready; ran `echo ok` over SSH; listed and stopped the exact claim; verified final inventory `[]` and no local-key residue.\n- Scaleway: authenticated from empty inventory; provisioned a real project/zone-bound instance and managed SSH key; reached ready; ran `echo ok` over SSH; listed and stopped the exact claim; verified final inventory `[]` and no managed-key residue.\n- Vultr: pending because an authenticated API credential is not yet available. Keep this PR unmerged until the same exact-head create/use/stop/empty-inventory proof passes for Vultr, or that provider-specific gate is explicitly waived.\n",
        "branch": "codex/issue811-provider-ownership",
